an ugly number is a number that does not have any prime factors other than 2, 3 or 5. what that implies is that any ugly number,
can be reduced to 1 by repeatedly dividing it by 2, 3 or 5 (if it is divisible by them that is). 
so what we do is, divide the number repeatedly by 2 till it is no longer divisible by it (i.e n%2!=0).
after that, repeatedly divide it by 3, till no longer divisible (i.e. n%3!=0) and repeat the same procedure for 5.
now after all these divisions (by 2, 3 and 5 - if valid) IF we have n reduced to 1
it implies that all the prime factors consitute of 2, 3 or 5; hence an ugly number (n == 1 is true)
however if n is not reduced to 1 by the end of our calculations
it implies that theres a factor other than 2, 3 or 5 
implying that n is not an ugly number (n == 1 is false)
